				<string>--- BUILD THE FILE CONTENTS ---

Get File above reads the running log at the fixed path with the file picker switched off and Error If Not Found switched off, so on the very first run it simply returns nothing instead of stopping the shortcut.

New Content is built inside the branches rather than by combining a separate Existing Log variable, because a Text action holding a genuinely empty string is not a permitted shape.

- If checks whether Get File returned anything
- When it did, Text joins the existing file first and the new log line second, so every earlier line is preserved, and New Content is set from that Text
- Otherwise Text holds only the new log line and New Content is set from that, which is what makes the very first run write a brand new file containing a single line
- Either way the join is plain concatenation with nothing between the two values, and no dictionary or list parsing is involved anywhere</string>
